{"id":"nld-t1-0011","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"count.zero","domain":2,"text_native":"nul","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"None, zero.","source_caption":"0","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Zero is the answer that gets misheard most often, because the word for nothing and the word for a small quantity are often unrelated.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0012","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"price.bill","domain":3,"text_native":"De rekening, alstublieft.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The bill, please.","source_caption":"The check, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Where the word for bill and the word for receipt are the same word and neither is 'account'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0013","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"price.card-ok","domain":3,"text_native":"{Flanders} Kan ik met een kredietkaart betalen?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Is card payment accepted?","source_caption":"Do you accept credit cards?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The alternative to carrying cash, and the question that decides whether you are standing in a queue that moves.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0014","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"price.cheaper","domain":3,"text_native":"Heeft u een goedkopere kamer?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Is there anything cheaper?","source_caption":"Do you have anything cheaper?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The follow-up that gets a different price rather than just a refusal.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0015","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"price.how-much","domain":3,"text_native":"Hoeveel kost dit?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How much is this?","source_caption":"How much is this?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most useful question in the tier, and the one people are most afraid to ask. It is not rude anywhere.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0016","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"goedkoop","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0017","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"Dat is te duur.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"That's too expensive.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0018","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"money.atm","domain":3,"text_native":"Waar vind ik een geldautomaat?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is an ATM?","source_caption":"Where is an automatic teller machine (ATM)?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognising rather than producing it: you will be shown the sign rather than expected to ask.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0019","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"money.change","domain":3,"text_native":"Kan u geld wisselen?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please change this into local money.","source_caption":"Can you change money for me?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The word 'change' means both coins and alteration in several of these languages, and the wrong one is confusing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0020","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"money.exchange-rate","domain":3,"text_native":"Wat is de wisselkoers?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"What is the exchange rate?","source_caption":"What is the exchange rate?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Often answered by pointing at a board rather than spoken.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0021","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"money.keep-change","domain":3,"text_native":"Hou het wisselgeld!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please keep the change.","source_caption":"Keep the change!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing loose coins is often faster and always understood.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba nld-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"848916","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0022","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"toilet.where","domain":12,"text_native":"Waar is het toilet?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the toilet?","source_caption":"Where is the toilet?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most urgent question in this tier and the one every phrasebook leads with. In several languages the word is the only one a traveller needs for years.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0023","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"food.menu","domain":4,"text_native":"Mag ik het menu, alstublieft?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The menu, please.","source_caption":"Can I look at the menu, please?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"One question covers a whole meal. Most phrasebooks waste slots on individual dishes instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0024","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"food.no-meat","domain":4,"text_native":"Ik eet geen varkensvlees.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I do not eat meat.","source_caption":"I don't eat pork.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying it once at the start of the trip saves a refusal at the table, where it is awkward for both sides.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0025","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"water","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0026","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"rechtdoor","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"straight ahead","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0027","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"Sla links af.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"Turn left.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0028","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"Sla rechts af.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"Turn right.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0029","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"way.where-to","domain":7,"text_native":"Hoe kom ik bij ...?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How do I get to","source_caption":"How do I get to ...?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Incomplete on its own — a name or a pointing gesture finishes it. That is how it is actually said.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0030","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"stay.checkout","domain":5,"text_native":"Ik wil vertrekken.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I would like to check out, please.","source_caption":"I want to check out.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said the morning before leaving, so the bill is not waiting at the desk while luggage is being gathered.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0031","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"stay.wifi","domain":5,"text_native":"Wat is het wifi-wachtwoord?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"What is the Wi-Fi password?","source_caption":"What is the WiFi password?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"A practical English loanword appears in most of these languages, so it is often easier than the local words for it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba nld-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"7459547","author":"andibing"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0032","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"move.destination","domain":6,"text_native":"Breng me erheen, alstublieft.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please take me there.","source_caption":"Take me there, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Shown with a map or a written address while saying it. 'There' is the word the pages use; 'this address' is in none of them, and a slot phrased from imagination rather than from a caption is a slot that can never be filled.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0033","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"move.taxi","domain":6,"text_native":"Bel een taxi alstublieft.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please call me a taxi.","source_caption":"Please call me a taxi.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Hailed rather than called in most of these countries, but asking produces one more option.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba nld-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"8922484","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0034","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"move.where-is-platform","domain":6,"text_native":"Op welk perron bevindt het zich?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Which platform?","source_caption":"Which platform is it on?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Answered by a sign or a display more often than by a person.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba nld-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"811196","author":"CM"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0035","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"shop.looking","domain":8,"text_native":"Ik ben alleen maar aan het kijken.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am just looking, thank you.","source_caption":"I'm just looking.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Buys the freedom to look without being followed by someone for twenty minutes. Not needed everywhere, and very needed in a few places.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba nld-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"4943438","author":"drnm2"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0036","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"Ik heb een dokter nodig.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0037","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"health.hospital","domain":9,"text_native":"Waar is het ziekenhuis?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the nearest hospital?","source_caption":"Where is the hospital?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asked of a passer-by rather than declared to a driver. The pages carry the question and not the instruction to be driven, which is a different conversation with a different person.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba nld-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"4172216","author":"CC"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0038","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"Blijf van me af!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0039","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"Het is een noodgeval.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0040","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"help.leave-me-alone","domain":10,"text_native":"Laat me met rust.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please leave me alone.","source_caption":"Leave me alone.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said firmly and quietly. Raising the volume is what turns it from a boundary into an incident in several of these cultures.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0041","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"Ik ben verdwaald.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0042","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"Mag ik uw telefoon gebruiken?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"nld-t1-0043","lang":"nld","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"Ik roep de politie.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"I'll call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Dutch phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Dutch_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
